00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:43,500
He will destroy the world. No man can stop him. No
man will even try. He is The Chosen.

2
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Holocaust 2000 is a science fiction, drama, horror
film directed by Alberto De Martino.

3
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:58,500
An executive in charge of a nuclear power plant in the Mid-East must stop his
son-- who turns out to be the Anti Christ -- from blowing it up.

4
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Robert Caine, played by Kirk Douglas.

5
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:13,500
Sara Golan, played by Agostina Belli.

6
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:51,000
Angel Caine, played by Simon Ward.

7
00:46:22,500 --> 00:46:28,500
Professor Griffith, played by Anthony Quayle.

8
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
Dr. Kerouac, played by Adolfo Celi.

9
00:59:37,500 --> 00:59:43,500
Charrier, played by Romolo Valli.

10
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:21,000
Holocaust 2000 (also released as The Chosen and Rain of Fire) is a 1977 horror film directed by Alberto De Martino, written by De Martino, Michael
Robson, and Sergio Donati, and starring Kirk Douglas, Simon Ward, Agostina Belli, Anthony Quayle, Virginia McKenna, and Alexander Knox.

11
01:12:52,500 --> 01:12:58,500
The original musical score was composed by Ennio Morricone.

12
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
The British-Italian co-production was produced by Edmondo Amati for The Rank Organisation and Titanus, and is
widely-considered a cash-in on the success of the similarly-themed The Omen, which was released a year earlier.

13
01:26:07,500 --> 01:26:13,500
It received mixed reviews, but has become a cult classic.

14
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:51,000
The film explores themes of nuclear power plant, nuclear holocaust, armageddon.

15
01:39:22,500 --> 01:39:28,500
The tone is dark and emotional and thought_provoking.
